  "source": {
    "title": "North Down Herald and County Down Independent, 17 January 1920, p. 1: \"Bangor Municipal Elections. Results of the Polling\" (Dufferin Electoral Area). First names and initials: Northern Whig, 17 January 1920, p. 6 (\"Bangor\").",
    "publisher": "North Down Herald (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "the elected in order, spoiled papers (14), quota (149) and every first preference as printed; the first preferences, several printed across a fold (Bailie 159, Fegan 104, Marshall 101, Thomson 16), add to 888, and 888 / 6 + 1 = 149, the printed quota. The poll is printed as 883 (or 863), which does not agree with 888 + 14, so it is not recorded. Transfers are not printed"
  },
  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Proportional representation (single transferable vote) under the Local Government (Ireland) Act 1919; polled 15 January 1920. Results declared 16 January 1920 by the returning officer, James Milliken (town clerk). The area returned 5 members, elected in the order (as printed) Wilson, Bailie, Neill, M'Millan, Fegan. Wilson, Neill and Bailie reached the quota on the first count; the counts at which M'Millan and Fegan were elected, and Marshall and Thomson eliminated, are not reported. The printed order puts Bailie (159) before Neill (161), which the figures as read do not explain. No report seen gives party labels."
